00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.440
Right now, we're watching an AI-generated Lego movie

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.180
out of Iran that depicts Trump as a war-hungry pedophile,

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:08.740
a video that's gone viral across the US and the world.

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:10.880
It's the work of an Iran-based group

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.400
called the Explosive News Team,

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.180
and the latest in a long line

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.160
of AI-generated Lego propaganda

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:19.260
aimed at mocking Donald Trump and Benjamin Netanyahu.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.740
And to be clear, Lego propaganda isn't new,

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:23.440
and the themes that the Iranian video

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.860
are pushing on aren't either.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.520
But in 2026, what is new is the speed

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:29.020
and the scale they're coming out at.

00:00:29.020 --> 00:00:31.920
During World War II, the Korean War, and the Vietnam War,

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:36.700
America's enemies littered the battlefield with pamphlets, cartoons, and radio broadcasts

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.640
aimed at shaking the morale of American troops.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.800
But that stuff rarely got back home.

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:44.800
Now, countries can use AI tools for dissemination across social media,

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:47.260
and in this case, against the U.S. home front.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:50.760
Iran has also shared videos of Trump drowning in a river of blood,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:53.320
all while the U.S. Department of Homeland Security are sharing

